{"alignments": [{"id": "1TI.2.1.a001", "note": "Inflected verb takes its supplied subject pronoun as a rule 7/9 helper; head on the lexical verb.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.001"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a002", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.002"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a003", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.003"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a004", "note": "Genitive with no determiner in the ASV: rule 21's determinerless clause keeps the case preposition *of* on the word itself.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.004"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a005", "note": "The ASV expands the infinitive into a finite clause; rule 85 gives the supplied complementizer *that* to the non-finite complement itself, discontinuously under rule 15. Head on the lexical verb *made*.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.005"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a006", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.006"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a007", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.007"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a008", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.008"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a009", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.009"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a010", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.010"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a011", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.011"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "1TI.2.1.a012", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.012"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.1.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}], "ref": "1TI.2.1", "review_notes": ["The four accusative nouns are split token for token under rule 26 rather than bundled as one list.", "*that … be made* is kept whole on the infinitive under rule 85; giving *that* to nothing (added) was rejected because a source token licenses the clause."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Greek projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "1TI.2.2.a001", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.001"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a002", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.002"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a003", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.003"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a004", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.004"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a005", "note": "Substantival article before a participle: rule 32 gives it the relativizing pronoun *that* and nothing else, the participle keeping its own verb.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.005"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a006", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.006"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a007", "note": "One Greek noun rendered by an adjective-plus-noun phrase. Under rules 66 and 91 *high* carries the lexeme's sense of eminence and *place* is the generic completion, so the head is *high*; a head on *place* as the phrase's formal noun remains defensible but rule 17 forbids choosing it on that ground alone.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.007"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a008", "note": "The copula is expressed in Greek, so rule 53 does not arise: *are* realizes the participle.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.008"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a009", "note": "Purpose conjunction realized by the word introducing its English clause (rule 40).", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.009"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a010", "note": "Attributive adjective only; rule 58 puts the supplied determiner on the expressed noun.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.010"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a011", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.011"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a012", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.012"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a013", "note": "Rule 58: both adjectives and the noun are anarthrous, so the supplied determiner *a* belongs to the noun, discontinuously under rule 15.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.013"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014", "t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a014", "note": "Subject and modal are rule 7/9 helpers on the inflected verb; head on the lexical verb.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.014"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a015", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.015"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a016", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.016"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a017", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.017"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a018", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.018"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "1TI.2.2.a019", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.019"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.2.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}], "ref": "1TI.2.2", "review_notes": ["The two *that* tokens are distinguished: t005 is the relativizer supplied for the substantival article, t010 the complementizer answering to ἵνα.", "*a tranquil and quiet life* is split token for token under rule 26, with the supplied determiner on the noun per rule 58."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Greek projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "1TI.2.3.a001", "note": "Verbless clause whose expressed subject is a substantival demonstrative: rule 68 puts it on rule 53's pronoun side, so *This is* stays together. Giving the copula to the adjectival predicate under rule 53's general clause is the competing reading, but rule 68 names this configuration expressly.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.001"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "1TI.2.3.a002", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.002"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "1TI.2.3.a003", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.003"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "1TI.2.3.a004", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.004"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "1TI.2.3.a005", "note": "Improper preposition with a complex supplied frame: rules 71 and 95 keep *in the sight of* whole and head it on the lexical noun *sight*, the trailing *of* riding with the frame as at REV.14.10.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.005"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006", "t007", "t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "1TI.2.3.a006", "note": "Rule 20: the genitive pronoun ἡμῶν occupies the determiner slot with *our*, so the article realizes nothing.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.006"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.006", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "1TI.2.3.a007", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.007"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "1TI.2.3.a008", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.008"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "1TI.2.3.a009", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.009"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}], "ref": "1TI.2.3", "review_notes": ["θεοῦ and σωτῆρος are split onto their own English words rather than sharing a head (rules 26, 28).", "The *the* of *the sight* belongs to the supplied frame, not to τοῦ, which stands before the genitive phrase the possessive has already determined."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Greek projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": [{"base_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.001"], "compatible_readings": ["r00-base"], "evidence": "ASV 2:3 begins \"This is good and acceptable\" with no inferential conjunction; the ASV renders γάρ as \"for\" where it stands, so the absence points to the base reading τοῦτο without γὰρ.", "fallback_used": false, "operational_reading": "r00-base", "projected_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.001"], "ref": "1TI.2.3", "selected_reading": "r00-base", "status": "selected", "unit_id": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.3.v001"}]}
{"alignments": [{"id": "1TI.2.4.a001", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.001"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "1TI.2.4.a002", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.002"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "1TI.2.4.a003", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.003"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "1TI.2.4.a004", "note": "*would have* renders the finite verb; rule 9 heads on the lexical verb rather than the modal.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.004"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "1TI.2.4.a005", "note": "Infinitival marker and copula are rule 7/9 helpers on the infinitive; head on the participial lexical verb.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.005"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006", "t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "1TI.2.4.a006", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.006"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "1TI.2.4.a007", "note": "Rule 36: the English preposition governing the phrase realizes the Greek preposition, not the verb.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.007"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "1TI.2.4.a008", "note": "Anarthrous Greek: rule 51's closing clause makes the supplied *the* an ordinary helper on the noun it determines.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.008"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "1TI.2.4.a009", "note": "Anarthrous genitive: the case preposition and the supplied determiner both ride with the noun under rules 21 and 51.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.009"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014", "t015", "t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "1TI.2.4.a010", "note": "The second infinitive shares the *to* of εἰς in the ASV's *come to the knowledge*, so the verb stands alone.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.010"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.4.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}], "ref": "1TI.2.4", "review_notes": ["No Greek article stands in this verse, so both English *the* tokens are supplied helpers on their nouns rather than article realizations."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Greek projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "1TI.2.5.a001", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.001"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a002", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.002"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a003", "note": "Verbless clause expressing no subject: rule 68 puts the supplied subject and copula on the predicate, and within the anarthrous adjective-plus-noun predicate the noun is the carrier (rule 58's reasoning). Putting *there is* on εἷς instead remains defensible.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.003"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003", "t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a004", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.004"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a005", "note": "Rule 65/70's English-side test: the ASV writes *also* for the particle.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.005"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a006", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.006"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a007", "note": "Rule 21's determinerless clause: the supplied case preposition *between* rides with the genitive noun.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.007"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a008", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.008"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a009", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.009"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a010", "note": "The ASV's supplied *himself* marks the appositive the noun heads, so it is folded as a rule 7 pronoun helper on ἄνθρωπος; rule 11 keeps the italics from deciding it. Marking *himself* `added` under rule 5, as rule 105 does for a supplied appositional word carried by an article, remains defensible.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.010"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a011", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.011"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "1TI.2.5.a012", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.012"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.5.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}], "ref": "1TI.2.5", "review_notes": ["The two εἷς tokens are kept on their own English *one* tokens rather than sharing one unit.", "Χριστός and Ἰησοῦς are split under rule 28 rather than given a shared head."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Greek projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "1TI.2.6.a001", "note": "Substantival article before a participle with a single English word: rule 90 gives the relativizer to the article, the participle keeping its own verb.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.001"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "1TI.2.6.a002", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.002"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "1TI.2.6.a003", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.003"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "1TI.2.6.a004", "note": "Anarthrous noun with a supplied determiner: rule 51's closing clause makes *a* a helper on the noun.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.004"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "1TI.2.6.a005", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.005"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "1TI.2.6.a006", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.006"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "1TI.2.6.a007", "note": "Rule 19: the article surfaces as *the*.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.007"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "1TI.2.6.a008", "note": "The ASV recasts the appositional phrase with a supplied verb; rule 92 puts the supplied words on the expressed predicate noun and leaves the article its bare determiner. Head on *testimony*, the word realizing the lexeme, the supplied *to be borne* realizing no source token.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.008"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010", "t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "1TI.2.6.a009", "note": "Rule 21's determinerless clause: the supplied case preposition *in* rides with the dative noun, discontinuously under rule 15.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.009"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "1TI.2.6.a010", "note": "Rule 47: ἴδιος is a source word able to take the supplied possessive, and here the noun is anarthrous so nothing competes.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.010"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.6.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}], "ref": "1TI.2.6", "review_notes": ["The supplied *to be borne* was kept on μαρτύριον under rule 92 rather than on the dative time phrase; nothing else in the appositional phrase is left unspent to carry it."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Greek projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "1TI.2.7.a001", "note": "Rule 35: the portmanteau spells both tokens, *where-* answering to the relative and *-unto* to the preposition; headed on the pronominal.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.001", "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.002"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a002", "note": "The subject is expressed, so only the passive auxiliary is a helper here.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.003"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a003", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.004"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a004", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.005"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a005", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.006"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a006", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.007"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a007", "note": "Anarthrous noun with a supplied determiner (rule 51).", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.008"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a008", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.009"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a009", "note": "Ordinary negative aligned to *not*; no negative indefinite stands, so rules 41 and 59 do not arise.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.010"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a010", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.011"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a011", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.012"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017", "t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a012", "note": "Anarthrous genitive: the case preposition and the supplied determiner ride with the noun under rules 21 and 51.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.013"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019", "t020", "t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a013", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.014"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a014", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.015"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a015", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.016"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024"], "target_head": "t024"}, {"id": "1TI.2.7.a016", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.017"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t025"], "target_head": "t025"}], "ref": "1TI.2.7", "review_notes": ["The three first-person subject pronouns are each kept with the verb whose inflection licenses them (rule 9); only t002 answers to the expressed ἐγώ.", "No Greek article stands in the verse, so both English *the* tokens are supplied helpers."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Greek projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": [{"base_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.009"], "compatible_readings": ["r00-base"], "evidence": "ASV 2:7 has the bare parenthesis \"(I speak the truth, I lie not)\" with no \"in Christ\"; a rendered ἐν Χριστῷ would be visible in the English, so the base λέγω is read.", "fallback_used": false, "operational_reading": "r00-base", "projected_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.009"], "ref": "1TI.2.7", "selected_reading": "r00-base", "status": "selected", "unit_id": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.7.v002"}]}
{"alignments": [{"id": "1TI.2.8.a001", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.001"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a002", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.002"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a003", "note": "The ASV expands the infinitive into a finite clause; rule 85 gives the supplied complementizer *that* to the complement rather than to the governing verb, discontinuously under rule 15.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.003"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a004", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.004"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a005", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.005"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a006", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.006"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a007", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.007"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a008", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.008"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a009", "note": "*up* is the English verb's own particle, not a separate source correspondence.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.009"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a010", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.010"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a011", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.011"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a012", "note": "Rule 101: the improper preposition is rendered by a single English word, so no trailing preposition or determiner question arises.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.012"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a013", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.013"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a014", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.014"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "1TI.2.8.a015", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.015"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}], "ref": "1TI.2.8", "review_notes": ["τοὺς ἄνδρας is split into article and noun under rules 19 and 26."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Greek projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": [{"base_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.015"], "compatible_readings": ["r00-base", "r01"], "evidence": "ASV \"without wrath and disputing\" uses an English mass noun that reflects neither singular διαλογισμοῦ nor plural διαλογισμῶν distinctly; the note \"Or, doubting\" is an alternative_rendering about English wording and cannot decide a reading.", "fallback_used": true, "operational_reading": "r00-base", "projected_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.015"], "ref": "1TI.2.8", "selected_reading": null, "status": "underdetermined", "unit_id": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.8.v003"}]}
{"alignments": [{"id": "1TI.2.9.a001", "note": "The adverb is rendered by the whole phrase *In like manner*. Head corrected from *manner* to *like*: rule 71's frame-heads-its-lexical-noun principle is scoped in terms to an improper preposition governing a case, and ὡσαύτως governs nothing, so that rule does not reach this unit. Rule 99 names the *manner* head as the recurring failure and treats *manner of* as a supplied frame, and rule 66's generic-completion test agrees — *like* carries the comparison the lexeme states and *manner* is the generic noun completing it, as *covetous man* heads on *covetous*. A head on *manner* as the phrase's nominal remains defensible, but rule 17 forbids choosing it merely for being the phrase's formal head.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.001"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a002", "note": "Rules 65 and 70's English-side test: the ASV writes no word for the adverbial καί.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.002"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.002", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a003", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.003"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a004", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.004"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a005", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.005"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a006", "note": "Attributive adjective split from its noun despite the ASV's reordering (rules 15, 26).", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.006"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a007", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.007"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a008", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.008"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a009", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.009"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a010", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.010"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a011", "note": "Rule 85: the supplied complementizer *that* belongs to the non-finite complement the ASV expands into a finite clause, discontinuously under rule 15.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.011"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a012", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.012"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a013", "note": "Ordinary negative aligned to *not*; the following words are not negative indefinites, so rule 59 does not arise.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.013"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a014", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.014"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a015", "note": "One Greek noun rendered by an adjective-plus-noun phrase: under rules 66 and 91 *braided* carries the plaiting sense of the lexeme and *hair* is the supplied generic completion, so the head is *braided*.", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.015"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017", "t018"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a016", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.016"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a017", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.017"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a018", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.018"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a019", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.019"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a020", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.020"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a021", "note": "", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.021"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.021", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t025"], "target_head": "t025"}, {"id": "1TI.2.9.a022", "note": "Adjective split from its noun despite the ASV's reordering (rules 15, 26).", "source": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.022"], "source_head": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.022", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024"], "target_head": "t024"}], "ref": "1TI.2.9", "review_notes": ["Head on ὡσαύτως corrected from *manner* to *like*; the unit's edges are unchanged. The competing reading is named in the unit note under rule 16.", "Noun and attributive adjective are split in both ἐν καταστολῇ κοσμίῳ and ἱματισμῷ πολυτελεῖ despite the ASV's reordering (rules 15, 26).", "The adverbial καί is `unrepresented` on rules 65 and 70's English-side test; a reference comparison will report it as a disagreement, and that report is not a correction."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Greek projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": [{"base_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.002"], "compatible_readings": ["r00-base", "r01", "r02"], "evidence": "ASV \"In like manner, that women adorn themselves\" shows no article (English generic plural takes none, so τὰς is invisible) and no \"also\", but the ASV routinely leaves adjunctive καί after ὡσαύτως unrendered; nothing in the English excludes any of the three readings.", "fallback_used": true, "operational_reading": "r00-base", "projected_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.002"], "ref": "1TI.2.9", "selected_reading": null, "status": "underdetermined", "unit_id": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.v004"}, {"base_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.016"], "compatible_readings": ["r00-base"], "evidence": "ASV 2:9 reads \"not with braided hair, and gold or pearls or costly raiment\": the connective between braided hair and gold is \"and\" while the following two are \"or\", so the ASV renders καὶ here, not ἢ.", "fallback_used": false, "operational_reading": "r00-base", "projected_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.016"], "ref": "1TI.2.9", "selected_reading": "r00-base", "status": "selected", "unit_id": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.v005"}, {"base_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.017"], "compatible_readings": ["r00-base", "r01"], "evidence": "χρυσίῳ and χρυσῷ are alike rendered \"gold\" in ASV 2:9; the English gives no purchase on the diminutive form.", "fallback_used": true, "operational_reading": "r00-base", "projected_source_ids": ["SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.017"], "ref": "1TI.2.9", "selected_reading": null, "status": "underdetermined", "unit_id": "SBLGNT.1TI.2.9.v006"}]}
